msgstr ""
"# Installation Guide\n"
"\n"
"## System Requirements\n"
"\n"
"Before installing, please ensure your system meets the following requirements:\n"
"\n"
"- **Operating System**: Windows 10/11, macOS 10.15 or later, or mainstream Linux distributions (such as Ubuntu 20.04, CentOS 8, etc.)\n"
"- **Memory**: At least 4GB of RAM (8GB or more is recommended)\n"
"- **Disk Space**: At least 2GB of available hard drive space\n"
"- **Network**: A stable internet connection is required for downloading dependencies and updates\n"
"\n"
"## Installation Steps\n"
"\n"
"### 1. Download the Installation Package\n"
"\n"
"Visit the official website to download the installation package that matches your operating system. The download address is: [https://example.com/download](https://example.com/download)\n"
"\n"
"### 2. Install Dependencies\n"
"\n"
"Some features require the following dependencies to be installed first:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"# For Debian/Ubuntu systems\n"
"sudo apt-get update\n"
"sudo apt-get install -y build-essential curl git\n"
"\n"
"# For CentOS/RHEL systems\n"
"sudo yum install -y gcc-c++ make curl git\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"### 3. Install the Main Program\n"
"\n"
"#### Windows System\n"
"\n"
"1. Double-click the downloaded `.exe` installation file\n"
"2. Follow the prompts in the installation wizard to complete the installation\n"
"3. During installation, you can choose the installation path and whether to create a desktop shortcut\n"
"\n"
"#### macOS System\n"
"\n"
"1. Open the downloaded `.dmg` file\n"
"2. Drag the application into the \"Applications\" folder\n"
"3. If you encounter a security prompt, go to \"System Preferences\" → \"Security & Privacy\" and click \"Open Anyway\"\n"
"\n"
"#### Linux System\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"# Decompress the installation package\n"
"tar -xzf example-app-linux-x64.tar.gz\n"
"\n"
"# Move to the installation directory\n"
"sudo mv example-app /opt/\n"
"\n"
"# Create a symbolic link\n"
"sudo ln -s /opt/example-app/bin/example-app /usr/local/bin/example-app\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"### 4. Environment Variable Configuration\n"
"\n"
"Add the following environment variables to the system configuration file (`~/.bashrc` or `~/.zshrc`):\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"export EXAMPLE_APP_HOME=\"/opt/example-app\"\n"
"export PATH=\"$EXAMPLE_APP_HOME/bin:$PATH\"\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"After saving, run the following command to make the configuration take effect:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"source ~/.bashrc\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"### 5. Verify the Installation\n"
"\n"
"Run the following command in the terminal to verify that the installation was successful:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"example-app --version\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"If the version information is displayed correctly, the installation is successful.\n"
"\n"
"## Common Issues\n"
"\n"
"### Issue 1: Permission Denied\n"
"\n"
"**Problem Description**: When running the program, a \"Permission denied\" error occurs.\n"
"\n"
"**Solution**: Check file permissions and ensure the execution permission is granted:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"chmod +x /opt/example-app/bin/example-app\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"### Issue 2: Missing Dynamic Link Library\n"
"\n"
"**Problem Description**: When starting the program, a prompt appears indicating that a `.so` or `.dll` file is missing.\n"
"\n"
"**Solution**: Install the corresponding dependency libraries:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"# For Debian/Ubuntu systems\n"
"sudo apt-get install -y libssl-dev libcurl4-openssl-dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"### Issue 3: Port Conflict\n"
"\n"
"**Problem Description**: The program fails to start because the default port is already occupied.\n"
"\n"
"**Solution**: Modify the port number in the configuration file, or use the following command to check which process is occupying the port:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"netstat -tulpn | grep 8080\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Uninstallation\n"
"\n"
"### Windows System\n"
"\n"
"Go to \"Control Panel\" → \"Programs and Features\", find the application, and click \"Uninstall\".\n"
"\n"
"### macOS System\n"
"\n"
"Move the application from the \"Applications\" folder to the Trash.\n"
"\n"
"### Linux System\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"sudo rm -rf /opt/example-app\n"
"sudo rm /usr/local/bin/example-app\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Technical Support\n"
"\n"
"If you encounter any issues during installation, please contact us through the following channels:\n"
"\n"
"- Official Documentation: [https://docs.example.com](https://docs.example.com)\n"
"- Community Forum: [https://forum.example.com](https://forum.example.com)\n"
"- Email Support: support@example.com\n"

msgid "安装指南"
msgstr "Installation Guide"

msgid "**Triton-Ascend**是适配华为Ascend处理器的Triton优化版本，主要用于提供高效的核函数自动调优、算子编译及部署能力，支持Ascend Atlas A2/A3/950系列产品，兼容Triton核心语法的同时，针对昇腾NPU特性进行了深度优化，包括自动解析核函数参数、优化内存访问逻辑、完善安全部署机制等。"
msgstr "**Triton-Ascend** is an optimized version of Triton adapted for Huawei Ascend processors, primarily designed to provide efficient kernel function auto-tuning, operator compilation, and deployment capabilities. It supports the Ascend Atlas A2/A3/950 series products, is compatible with the core syntax of Triton, and has been deeply optimized for the features of the Ascend NPU, including automatic parsing of kernel function parameters, optimization of memory access logic, and enhancement of secure deployment mechanisms."

msgid "环境准备"
msgstr "Environment Setup"

msgid "**硬件要求**"
msgstr "**Hardware Requirements**"

msgid "Ascend产品：支持Atlas A2/A3/950系列。"
msgstr "Ascend Products: Support Atlas A2/A3/950 series."

msgid "NPU配置：建议至少单卡32GB内存。"
msgstr "NPU Configuration: It is recommended to have at least 32GB of memory per single card."

msgid "操作系统：需Linux系统，具体请参考<a href=\"https://www.hiascend.com/hardware/compatibility\" style=\"text-decoration: none; color: #0066cc;\">兼容性查询助手</a>。本文接下来所有操作均以**Ubuntu**环境演示。"
msgstr "Operating System: Linux is required. For details, please refer to the <a href=\"https://www.hiascend.com/hardware/compatibility\" style=\"text-decoration: none; color: #0066cc;\">Compatibility Query Assistant</a>. All subsequent operations in this document are demonstrated in the **Ubuntu** environment."

msgid "**软件依赖**"
msgstr "**Software Dependencies**"

msgid "确定CANN、Python和TorchNPU软件版本并安装。其中，可以参考昇腾社区官网《[CANN快速安装](https://www.hiascend.com/cann/download)》 完成驱动与固件安装。"
msgstr "Determine the software versions of CANN, Python, and TorchNPU and install them. For driver and firmware installation, refer to the Ascend Community official website's [CANN Quick Installation](https://www.hiascend.com/cann/download)."

msgid "CANN版本：9.0.0"
msgstr "CANN version: 9.0.0"

msgid "Python版本：python3.11"
msgstr "Python version: python3.11"

msgid "TorchNPU版本：2.7.1.post4"
msgstr "TorchNPU version: 2.7.1.post4"

msgid "注：更多配套关系请参考[版本说明表](./release_note.md#版本兼容性矩阵)。"
msgstr "Note: For more compatibility information, refer to the [Release Notes](./release_note.md#version-compatibility-matrix)."

